        "subject": "LU-21149 ptlrpc: serialize ping evictor start and stop",
        "message": "LU-21149 ptlrpc: serialize ping evictor start and stop\n\nping_evictor_start() and ping_evictor_stop() changed pet_refcount\nwithout a lock, and each start reinitialized pet_waitq.  Since\ntargets on one server are mounted in parallel, two mounts can each\nstart an ll_evictor thread, or reinitialize the wait queue under a\nthread already sleeping on it so it is never woken.  The orphaned\nthread holds its lu_env, which pins mdd, osp and mdt, so rmmod\nfails with \"Module mdd is in use\" (sanity-sec test_31).  A start\nsoon after the last stop could also run a second thread on\npet_list while the first was still emptying it.\n\nProtect the count with a mutex, initialize the wait queue once, and\nlet a start revive a thread that has not yet exited rather than\nstart another.  A revived thread can find pet_list empty after its\nwakeup, so it goes back to waiting instead of taking an entry.\n\nThis was split from https://review.whamcloud.com/64202, where an\nMGS follower stopping and starting on failover hit the same race.\n\nTest-Parameters: mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=sanity-sec env=ONLY=31,ONLY_REPEAT=10\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I8fa09b077cf24e8b9b29bc0b8929b272a3d97d6d\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master",
      "description": "Edit commit message"
    }
